name sat-07-dry-merge-1
timeout 520
time 1991-01-19T08:00:00Z
wx fixture wx-2026-07-27T00Z.wxb

# MEASURING RIG, NOT A CAMPAIGN RUNG. `sat-*` files belong to no `.fbc`, are named by no campaign and
# move no doctrine. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md; the criteria: doc/doctrine-evolution.md 4.2.
#
# THE MARGIN, IN THE HEAD, AS A NUMBER: every graded quantity in this file is a declared-cylinder
# DWELL, its threshold sits in a MEASURED gap of that dwell's own lever spectrum, and the narrowest of
# those gaps is 3.20 s against a MEASURED chaos amplitude of 0.30 s over the +-3 m spawn grid —
# **11x**. The widest is 146.45 s against 0.10 s (1 464x). Nothing here is graded within 10x of the
# coin.
#
# WHAT MAKES THE AMPLITUDE THAT SMALL, and it is the one structural idea of this file: THE ENGAGEMENT
# IS DRY. Both sides carry `brief_master_arm sim`, so the hardware refuses every launch — [MESS] 63
# `sms RELEASE_REJECTED reason=hardware_precedence`, 0 `damage KILL`, 0 `monitor KO` in the baseline.
# Sorting, locking, cranking, the RWR answer and the emission discipline all run exactly as they do in
# a live merge; what is removed is the DISCRETE EVENT that amplifies a 3 m perturbation into a bit. The
# consequence is measured, not argued: sat-04's belt dwell moves 1.0 s over the same grid, this file's
# moves 0.10..0.30 s. `survive` is met by every unit on every lever and is therefore a CONSTANT rather
# than the coin doc/doctrine-evolution.md 4b names.
#
# THE THREE GRADED DEVICES, each with its own measurement:
#   1. `zone zb` — a 10 km cylinder across the merge, graded on `sw2` by a SIX-RUNG exposure ladder
#      (20.6 / 46.5 / 76.8 / 92.8 / 112.8 / 122.2 s) and on `sw3`/`sw4` by one rung each. [MESS, 25
#      lever runs] sw2's dwell takes 10 distinct values from 0.0 to 125.4 s; every rung sits at the
#      MIDPOINT of a gap in that spectrum, half-gaps 6.35 / 19.55 / 4.35 / 11.55 / 6.15 / 3.20 s.
#      WHY A LADDER AND NOT ONE THRESHOLD: the outcome class is (V, M) and M is a SUM, so a lever that
#      changes WHICH bit is met without changing HOW MANY is invisible to it. A monotone rung ladder on
#      one continuous quantity turns that quantity into a COUNT, which is what the class can see.
#   2. `zone zs` — the same cylinder question asked in the vertical: a 6 600..9 000 m band that only a
#      flight flying the WIDE altitude stack ever enters. [MESS] sw1's ceiling is 6 061 m at the seed
#      and 7 603 m under `shape-stacked`; the band floor is 539 m above the highest non-stacked run.
#   3. THE RELEASE GATE — a CCIP pair on two soft aim points. `ccip-tight` refuses the release
#      OUTRIGHT (2 releases -> 0), which is a STRUCTURAL move and not a lattice one.
#
# THE AIM POINTS ARE AT THE FIXED POINT OF THEIR OWN RELEASE LATTICE, and that is not the same thing as
# the midpoint of the printed impacts: the pilot's CCIP solution is computed against the DESIGNATED
# target, so moving the target moves the impact with a gain below 1 and a one-shot placement does not
# centre it. Iterated to convergence (tools of the round, 2 iterations): [MESS] the baseline impact
# lands 0.0 m from the target and the two bias rails +-23.7 m along track, against the Mk 82's 45 m
# fail radius — 21.3 m of margin on both sides. `bias-early` and `bias-late` are therefore INERT here,
# which is doc/doctrine-evolution.md 4a's arithmetic satisfied rather than evaded: a 23 m lever may not
# grade a 45 m radius, so this file does not ask it to.
#
# GENE FAMILIES, MEASURED (the arena's own table, 25 levers, `--elev const`):
#   live    G5 emcon 3 of 3:  emcon-mid (17,18)  emcon-tight (16,18)  emcon-wide (16,14)
#   live    G1 shape 4 of 6:  shape-abreast (18,21)  shape-stacked (14,16)  shape-tight (17,19)
#                             shape-wide (17,15);  shape-flat and shape-trail INERT
#   live    G3 net   1 of 2:  net-off (16,18);  `sort-left`/`sort-near` are dead beside a live net
#   live    G7 ccip  1 of 2:  ccip-tight (15,15), 0 releases;  ccip-open INERT
#   part    G6 bias  1 of 3:  `bias-rail` only (15,15) — 2.3 km of track, i.e. no delivery at all, and
#                             therefore NOT a mover anybody may read as a direction
#   INERT   G2 cover 0 of 3:  the AIM-120 binds 0.3 s — inert by AIRFRAME, not by this file
#   INERT   G4 energy 0 of 3: it lives only inside `Phase::Bfm`, and no unit here flies `set task bfm`
#   BASELINE (17, 17), duration 520.0 s.  10 movers of 24, 9 of them excluding `bias-rail`; 9 distinct
#   classes; modal share 60.0 % (15 of 25) — AT the S1 bound, with no slack, and that is stated rather
#   than smoothed: the 14 levers that are the identity map plus the baseline ARE 60 % of this lever
#   file, so no cell built against it can go below that without an 11th mover.
#   S7: [MESS] **0 of 8** spawn perturbations on the 0.8 m grid flip the baseline class.
#
# AND THE CLOCK, because X-7 is the trap this rig is built against: the run duration takes exactly two
# values over the lever set, 520.0 s (the timeout) and 300.1 s (`shape-abreast`, where every unit had
# concluded because every window had closed). The second is not a truncation — 300.1 s IS the instant
# every objective in this file was frozen at, so nothing graded could still have moved.
#
# THE ARENA: four F-16 sweeping east against eight MiG-29 under a GCI brief, plus a CCIP pair on two
# soft aim points. `--elev const`, 0 m datum, no terrain masking (C4). `wx fixture` is the committed
# GFS blob. Day, 11:00 local. Every coordinate is [SET] except the two aim points, which are the
# converged fixed point above. THE SUBSTITUTION AND ITS DIRECTION: the MiG-29 is the strongest
# Soviet-pattern fighter in the tree, so RED is stronger here than any historical eight-ship this
# geometry resembles. This file is an instrument, not a rung.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: IN A MERGE WHERE NOBODY CAN SHOOT, DOES THE FLIGHT'S OWN SHAPE AND
# EMISSION POLICY DECIDE WHERE IT SPENDS ITS TIME?
#
# WHAT TO READ:
#   events.log         `mission WINDOW_CLOSED` — one line per declared span, the frozen state, at
#                      t = 300.1; `zone ENTER`/`EXIT`; `sms RELEASE_REJECTED` (the dry proof);
#                      `stores DELIVERY` and `damage DAMAGE ... bodyFwdM/bodyRightM` (the lattice)
#   telemetry_sw*.csv  `zone_zb_s`, `zone_zs_s` — the two dwells the ladders read
#
# READING RULE, BINDING: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the EXPECTED exit and is NOT the measurement; a duration
# below 520 s is not one either, because it can only be the instant the last window closed. THE
# MEASUREMENT IS (V, M) SUMMED OVER THE SIX F-16 — 13 `avoid zone` rungs, 2 `kill unit` and 6
# `survive`, 21 objectives — AND ITS SPREAD ACROSS THE LEVER SET. A single run of this file measures
# NOTHING. A reader who quotes `bias-rail` as a direction has quoted a lever that deletes the delivery.

zone zb 33.10000 44.50000 10000 0 12000
zone zs 33.20000 44.50000 60000 6600 9000

unit sw1
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight sw 1
  spawn 33.20000 43.90000 6000 90.0 480
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set datalink on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm sim
  set task intercept
  wp 33.20000 45.10000 6000 480
  objective avoid zone zs exposure 61.5 until 300
  objective survive until 300

